  "body": "Part of #894.\n\n#894's first slice adds two tool kinds and two `Thread` operation fields that the MCP tools already carry through their JSON shapes - `add_tool` takes `\"kind\": \"thread_mill\"` / `\"thread_mill_single\"` (with `pitch`, `pitch_min`, `tip_angle`) or the catalog names `TM-0600-P125` / `TMS-0600-P050-150`; `add_operation` / `edit_operation` take the Thread params `pitch` and `hand` - pinned by `thread_milling_over_the_tools` in `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`.\n\nThe `camcraft-mcp` skill text (`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/`) does not mention them, so an agent reading the skill does not learn that a Thread operation now needs a thread-mill tool (a Tap is refused), that a single-form mill needs the pitch stated, or that hole radii are the thread's minor radius.\n\n**Done means:** the skill's tool-kind and parameter reference lists the two thread-mill kinds, `pitch_min`, and the Thread operation's `pitch` / `hand` with the refusals an agent will meet; `PROCESS_VERSION` bumped (the skill is a process file) and announced on #681.\n",
